The original failure is caused by `appendQuotedString(...)` returning from this branch without advancing `pos`:

```java
if (escapingOn && c[start] == QUOTE) {
    return appendTo == null ? null : appendTo.append(QUOTE);
}
```

At the `applyPattern` call site, that means the outer loop sees the same quote again and again, repeatedly appends, and eventually blows up with `OutOfMemoryError`.

The patch changes that to:

```java
if (escapingOn && c[start] == QUOTE) {
    next(pos);
    return appendTo == null ? null : appendTo.append(QUOTE);
}
```

That directly fixes the root cause: the parser now makes progress whenever it handles that leading escaped-quote case.

I do not see another concrete input that still reaches the same non-advancing / infinite-growth fault in this region after this change. The problematic branch was exactly the one leaving `pos` unchanged, and the patch removes that condition.

So this is not merely tailored to the one test; it fixes the underlying cause of the reported OOM.

